{"id": "EUVD-2026-70788", "enisaUuid": "0c97daba-17ca-3797-9def-5d5a4ce2b83d", "description": "MOOS core-moos through 10.4.0 contains a buffer overflow vulnerability in CMOOSSerialPort::GetTelegram() that writes a NUL terminator one byte past the serial telegram stack buffer. Attackers controlling the serial line can send a full-length telegram to trigger the off-by-one write, corrupting the stack and potentially enabling code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-09-03T22:38:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-08T13:57:18", "baseScore": 5.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:P/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/themoos/core-moos/pull/73", "https://github.com/themoos/core-moos/commit/befb04df2039d0080715ea35f56268092db4ec0f", "https://github.com/themoos/core-moos", "https://github.com/themoos/core-moos/blob/ec9c77c68fcbdef8f5e4c60fe243acd223433f0c/Core/libMOOS/Utils/MOOSSerialPort.cpp#L595", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/moos-core-moos-through-10.4.0-off-by-one-buffer-overflow-in-serial-telegram-handling"], "aliases": ["GHSA-793h-4m99-4gx3", "CVE-2026-85454"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7daae23c-0d8b-3c0b-91dc-cd6db0a7de87", "product": {"name": "core-moos", "vendor": {"name": "themoos"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226410.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f5364600-e842-3e8d-9cf9-7d574fdf43bf", "vendor": {"name": "themoos"}}], "isExploited": false}